ground truth (exp01) and large-replicate power analysis (exp02/03).

Two facts about the RTX 5090 drive every downstream choice:
  32 GiB, not 80 GiB  -> DMD-style training holds 3 backbone copies; with fp32
                         Adam that is 16 B/param/trainable copy. Sets a hard
                         ~850M param ceiling for 2 trainable copies.
  NO NVLink           -> FSDP all-gathers every layer over PCIe 5 (~50 GB/s vs
                         900 GB/s). This is an ARCHITECTURE decision, not a perf
                         note: use DDP with full local replicas wherever they
                         fit; ZeRO-2 before ZeRO-3; full FSDP only for SDXL.

Built ddgpu/memcalc.py to DERIVE the budget rather than guess it: parameter
counts come from instantiating ddgpu/dit.py on the meta device (verified against
the DiT paper: S 32.9M / B 130.3M / L 457.8M / XL 674.8M -- exact match),
memory from an explicit byte accounting, wall-clock from a FLOP model at 38% MFU.
Wrote ddgpu/probe.py to MEASURE peak VRAM and step time on the real card, because
the activation term is the one number I cannot validate without a GPU. RUNPLAN.md
says explicitly that if the probe disagrees, the probe wins.

Headline allocation: ONE 8x5090 NODE, ~2 weeks, covers the whole ImageNet story.
Blockers the calculator surfaced that I would otherwise have hit at launch time:
  - SDXL full finetune needs 81.3 GiB of state. Impossible on 32 GiB at ANY GPU
