[2026-08-19 | ENTRY 004 | TRACK B BUG FOUND BY ITS OWN DIAGNOSTICS -- keep this]
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
First Track B smoke run reported:
    eff_rank_frac=0.056   z_std=0.00084   mmd/ksd/mom pinned at constants
i.e. the encoder was outputting EXACTLY ZERO and not moving.

Cause: DiT zero-initialises its final layer. That is standard and CORRECT for a
denoiser, because the EDM skip connection c_skip*x carries the signal at init.
The encoder E has no such skip -- so a zero-init E outputs identically zero,
which IS the fully-collapsed encoder. The degenerate solution that Track B's
whole design is meant to avoid was being handed to the optimiser as its
STARTING POINT, and the Gaussianity gradient at exactly z=0 is uninformative.

Fix: give E a skip. E(x) = (x/sigma_data + net(x/sigma_data)) * sigma_max, so at
init E is a whitening map (z has std sigma_max when x has std sigma_data) and
the network learns the residual. After the fix: eff_rank_frac 0.056 -> 0.88,
z_std 0.00084 -> 2.2.

This is worth recording for two reasons. First, it would have burned a full
multi-day 8-GPU run before anyone noticed, because the loss curves looked fine --
only the rank diagnostic showed it. Second, it argues the diagnostics were
correctly chosen: effective rank of E#p_data is a leading indicator of collusion
and moves long before FID does. Keep diag_every small early in every Track B run.

Also fixed while here: teacher_ode had dead code and started its reverse pass at
sigma=0 where the PF-ODE drift is undefined -- inversion now runs sigma_min to
sigma_max. And eff_rank was normalised by d when a batch of B can span at most
min(B,d) dimensions, which made the number meaningless whenever B < d.

