FINDING 8 -- the cross-GPU all-gather of z is worth doing and now has a number
  attached. Per-device micro-batch is 64-128; gathered over 8 GPUs it is 512.
  For KSD's one genuine capability (correlation structure) that is power 0.12 ->
  0.76. The all-gather costs a (B,d) tensor, ~2 MB, i.e. nothing. Implemented in
  invertible.py:gaussianity and, for the same reason, in robust.py for Track A's
  REAL BATCH -- V_B ~ 1/N, so gathering multiplies the effective N by world size
  and is the cheapest quality lever in Track A.

