  flat at chance from B=64 to B=512. So it is not a sample-size problem that
  more compute fixes; it is a genuine limitation of these statistics. Reinforces
  ENTRY 005 FINDING 6: the teacher anchor is the only defence.

TWO BUGS found by reading the code rather than running it -- both would have
surfaced only on multi-GPU, i.e. only after committing a node:
  (a) `self.mu.score(...)` in dmd2.dm_loss. DDP does not forward attribute
      access to the wrapped module, so this is AttributeError the moment
      world_size > 1, and works fine in every single-GPU smoke test. Fixed via
      an explicit _raw() unwrap.
  (b) multiple grad-tracked forwards of one module per backward. The few-step
      student calls G once per step; Track B calls G and E on three legs each.
      DDP's reducer marks a parameter ready on its first autograd hook and
      raises on the second. Fixed two ways: the few-step generator now runs all
      but one randomly chosen step under no_grad (which is what DMD2 does
      anyway), and Track B's DDP wrappers are built with static_graph=True.
  Recording these because they are the class of bug that a single-GPU smoke test
  is structurally incapable of catching, and the first multi-GPU launch is
  exactly when the budget starts burning.

Also added since ENTRY 003:
  - ddgpu/gan.py + DiT.trunk(): DMD2's auxiliary discriminator as a head on the
    critic's own features. The baseline must be the REAL DMD2, not a weakened
    DMD -- Track A's claim is that this term can be replaced, and that claim is
    worthless if the thing it replaces is a strawman. gan_weight=1e-3 in the
    baseline configs, 0 in Track A's.
  - the low-noise gate now SKIPS computing the empirical score rather than
    down-weighting it. Beyond the ~40% compute saving there is a correctness
    reason: cdist forms ||a||^2+||b||^2-2a.b, which at d=16384 carries ~1e-3
    absolute error; divided by 2 sigma^2 at sigma=0.01 that is an O(10)
    perturbation of the softmax logits, so the nearest-neighbour weights are
    essentially arbitrary. Cheaper AND more correct.
  - ddgpu/generate.py: sampling + FID + precision/recall, reading gpu_seconds
    out of the checkpoint so the matched-wall-clock guard can be enforced.
  - exp/06_toy_distill.py: end-to-end distillation on the GMM, where mode
    coverage is EXACT (closed-form component posteriors) rather than approximated
    by precision/recall. Queued.

