FINDING 10 -- KSD's power against CORRELATION structure improves with BOTH
  dimension and batch size, reaching 0.98 at d=16384/B=512. This is the opposite
  of the usual "kernel methods die in high dimension" story, and it is the one
  place where the Stein machinery of idea #1 clearly earns its keep. It is also
  a concrete argument for the cross-GPU all-gather: at a per-device micro-batch
  of 64 the same statistic has power 0.21.
  Caveat before this gets over-claimed: the target here is N(0,I) with an EXACT
  linear score. Nothing in exp02/03 speaks to KSD against a data distribution
  whose score comes from a network -- which is the setting info.txt warned about,
  and which these experiments deliberately do not test.

FINDING 11 -- the picture across exp02+exp03, as a design rule for Track B:
    moment penalty  -> rank collapse, scale.        Power 1.0 everywhere, O(Bd).
    MMD (h^2 = d)   -> scale (needs B >= 256).      Redundant with moment.
    KSD             -> correlation only, wants big B and big d.
    nothing         -> mixture / matched-moment non-Gaussianity.
  So the honest weighting is: moment as the workhorse, KSD for what only it
  sees, MMD as cheap insurance. And the teacher anchor for the gap none of them
  cover. Configs updated accordingly is a TODO for the first GPU sweep -- the
  current weights (w_mmd=10, w_ksd=1, w_moment=10) were set before this evidence
  and should be revisited against it.

