(C) OFF-DISTRIBUTION EVALUATION POINTS. The objection I most expected to matter,
    and it does -- but it revises the story rather than breaking it.
    In real distillation the score is queried at STUDENT samples. Simulating a
    student three ways at d=128, N=256:

      kind      lam* at low sigma   var_B/||s||^2   bias_A/||s||^2   oracle gain
      ondist          1.00              90.8            0.032           1.00
      blurred         0.76               0.6            0.376           0.63
      shifted         0.77               0.6            0.372           0.63
      shrunk          0.58               0.6            0.852           0.42

