  1.00 and 0.76). So the sigma gate, which is what makes the method safe, also
  forfeits most of the off-distribution gain:
      shrunk:  oracle mean 0.651 (best 0.415)  vs shipped 0.926 (best 0.573)
  That is ~28% of available improvement left on the table exactly where the
  student is worst. It is a well-posed open problem, not a mystery: the missing
  quantity is <b_B, u>, the term lam_hat drops. A Richardson-style extrapolation
  in N (comparing B estimated at N and 2N) is the obvious attack and is cheap,
  since both are already computed for the half-batch variance estimate. NOT
